 #uuid "0df94000-eea7-560d-be59-c18037122c7c" 13194139535227 17592186045443 true] [17592186482661 1068 #edb/ref 17592186482679 13194139535227 17592186045443 true] [17592186482661 1068 #edb/ref 17592186482698 13194139535227 17592186045443 true] [17592186482661 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535227 17592186045443 true] [17592186482661 1071 "Find the equation of the line that passes through the point $(-2,-1)$ and is parallel to $8x + 2y = 1$. Write your answer in **standard form.** Use $Ax+By=C$ with integer $A,B,C$, $A>0$, and coprime $A$ and $B$ (their greatest common divisor is $1$). Enter $Ax+By$ in the first blank and $C$ in the second blank.\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=$\n{{field-2}}" 13194139535227 17592186045443 true] [17592186482661 1072 #uuid "0f9dba79-4d85-500f-864d-6679c1dd4ec3" 13194139535227 17592186045443 true] [17592186482661 1074 "Since parallel lines have equal slopes, both lines should have the same slope.\n\nFirst, write the given line in slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8 x + 2 y &= 1 \\\\ 2 y &= 1 -8 x \\\\ y &= \\frac{1}{2} -4 x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we wish to find a line that has a slope of $-4$ and passes through the point $(-2,-1)$. To find the equation of this line, we use point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 &= m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(-1) &= -4(x-(-2)) \\\\ y-(-1) &= -4 x -8 \\\\ y &= -4 x -9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, write the equation in standard form with coprime integer coefficients and a positive $x$-coefficient.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -4 x -9 \\\\ 4 x + y &= -9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe first blank is $4 x + y$ and the second blank is $-9$." 13194139535227 17592186045443 true] [17592186482662 1075 #edb/ref 17592186482680 13194139535227 17592186045443 true] [17592186482662 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139535227 17592186045443 true] [17592186482662 1077 "field-2" 13194139535227 17592186045443 true] [17592186482662 1078 #edb/ref 17592186482680 13194139535227 17592186045443 true] [17592186482662 1079 #uu